  "body": "*Copy-pasting my message from Matrix:*\r\n\r\nSince Resource-Hints [has been archived](https://github.com/w3c/resource-hints/issues/100) and now points to HTML, it's not clear to me if dynamically inserted `<link rel=\"prefetch\">` are supposed to work or if only the ones in the initial parsing would? It [used to be](https://web.archive.org/web/20210812122804/https://w3c.github.io/resource-hints/#fetching-the-resource-hint-link) explicitly stated\r\n\r\n>    The resource hint link's [...] MAY be dynamically added to and removed from the document.\r\n\r\nIt was even [one of the use-cases](https://web.archive.org/web/20210812122804/https://w3c.github.io/resource-hints/#reactive-resource-prefetching-prefetch) in that document.\r\n\r\nDid I just miss where the current specs would allow that? I was hoping for *allowed in body* to say something related but even looking at that I didn't find anything conclusive.\r\n\r\n___\r\n\r\nAs a response, @domenic  pointed out that `prefetch` might be missing an \"appropriate times to fetch and process\".   \r\n\r\nBut I kind of wonder if my initial case wasn't actually more related to #8138 anyway, cc @noamr.",
